IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 6798 of 2019
CITATION: 2020 SCC OnLine SC 1012
YEAR: 2020

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: L. Nageswara Rao, Hemant Gupta

PARTIES:
Rajneesh Kumar vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Persons with Disabilities Act, 1995, Rights of Persons with Disabilities Act, 2016

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 33 PwD Act, Article 16

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
reservation for disabled, promotions in government jobs, reasonable accommodation

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Reaffirmed reservation for persons with disabilities in public employment promotions, mandating reasonable accommodation as a facet of substantive equality.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 33 PwD Act, Article 16.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

